        passageEn:
            "In the Nova School class group chat, Thiha noticed several classmates mocking Zin Min's drawing, posting unkind comments about it one after another.\n\nThiha remembered what Ms. Thanda had taught about the difference between a bystander, who watches and does nothing, and an upstander, who takes action. Instead of staying silent, he posted a supportive comment praising Zin Min's drawing and gently reminded the group that unkind comments were not allowed in the class chat.\n\nAfterwards, Thiha also messaged Zin Min privately to check how he was feeling, and reported the unkind messages to Ms. Thanda so the situation could be handled properly. Zin Min later told Thiha that his one supportive comment had made the whole situation feel less overwhelming, proving that a small act of kindness online could make a real difference.",
        passageMy:
