            "For the Term 7 capstone, Thiha's class was asked to build a Nova School Digital Yearbook page, combining everything they had learned about networks, search skills, and cloud collaboration.\n\nFirst, the class needed accurate facts about the school's history for the yearbook, so Thiha used specific keywords and quotation marks in a search engine to find the exact founding date, avoiding the vague single-word searches that used to give him thousands of unrelated results.\n\nNext, the whole class worked together on a shared cloud document, with different students adding photos, quotes, and stories about the year at the same time from their own homes, watching each other's cursors move across the page in real time. When the document needed a certain student's private information removed, they simply edited the shared file, and the change synced instantly for everyone.\n\nFinally, when the yearbook page was ready to publish, the class understood that clicking \"publish\" would send it out across the internet -- broken into data packets, carried through routers and servers -- to reach every family's device, no matter how far away they lived. Thiha realized that networks, search skills, and cloud tools were not three separate lessons anymore; they were all working together, just like in the real world.",
