        titleEn: "Thiha Prepares His Portfolio for Year 6",
        titleMy: "သီဟ Year 6 အတွက် သူ့ portfolio ကို ပြင်ဆင်ခြင်း",
        passageEn:
            "Before the final Computing exam, Ms. Thanda asked every student to build a small portfolio folder showing one artifact from each term of the year, and Thiha spent an evening choosing his favorites.\n\nFrom Term 1, he picked a screenshot of his very first working quiz game, complete with the buggy score variable he later learned to rename. From Terms 2 and 3, he chose a flowchart showing a loop counting down a rocket launch. From Term 4, he added the selection logic from his fair ticket kiosk project.\n\nHe was especially proud of his Term 5 and 6 choices: a diagram explaining how his readingMinutes variable worked, next to a short note on how computers represent that same number as binary. For Term 7, he included a screenshot of the Nova School Digital Yearbook page his team had built together in the cloud, and for Term 8, a photo of his Smart Garden control box with its three sensors.\n\nLooking at the finished portfolio, Thiha noticed something Ms. Thanda had said all year: every project connected to the ones before it. His Term 8 sensors used the same IPO cycle as his Term 7 network, which delivered messages built from the same binary data he had studied in Term 6, tracked by the same kind of variables from Term 5, inside programs built from the same loops and conditions from Terms 2 through 4 -- and it had all started with the safe, responsible habits from Term 1.",
        passageMy:
