/// Secondary 3 (Year 9) Computing -- Term 7: "Software Engineering
/// Principles". Introduces the five-stage SDLC -- requirements
/// analysis, design, coding, testing, maintenance -- and the cost of
/// skipping early stages (Week 25), covers black-box/white-box testing
/// and normal/boundary/erroneous test data, tied to unit tests (Week
/// 26), then introduces Git version control -- commits, push/pull,
/// branching -- for safe collaboration (Week 27), closing with a
/// capstone week (Week 28, a boss week) that simulates a real
/// open-source contribution: requirements-first understanding, a
/// boundary-data-driven test for a bug fix, Git's branch/commit/push
/// workflow, documentation, a pull request, and code review before
/// merge.
