      "The Year 6 Computing course follows Nay Chi, a Nova School student, across a full academic year. Term 1 covers text-based coding basics, including variables and loops. Term 2 covers building a web page with HTML. Term 3 covers spreadsheets and data handling, including formulas. Term 4 covers databases, including records and fields. Term 5 covers a game creation project, including sprites and game loops. Term 6 covers physical computing and sensors, including actuators. Term 7 covers networks and how the internet works, including the client-server model and search engines. Term 8 covers data representation, including binary, images, and sound. Term 9 reviews the whole year's concepts and closes with the Year 6 Computing Graduation, in which Nay Chi presents a final project combining every skill from the year.",
