        passageEn:
            "The whole school gathers for the Year 1 Computing Graduation Showcase, where Moe Moe, Nay Chi, and Htet Htet each present a project combining everything they learned this year.\n\nMoe Moe's project is a digital drawing: a house made with shape tools (Term 4), decorated with a repeating red-blue border pattern (Term 6), with a typed title \"My House\" using shift for the capital M and H (Term 8).\n\nNay Chi's project is a robot demonstration: she writes a bug-free step-by-step sequence (Term 3) to guide her toy robot around the classroom, then explains to the audience why keeping her password private (Term 5) matters just as much as her robot's directions being correct.\n\nHtet Htet's project ties together computer basics (Term 1), sorting (Term 2), and hidden computers (Term 7): he sorts a table of gadgets into \"has a hidden computer\" and \"no hidden computer,\" then explains that a computer's screen and keyboard are input and output just like the ones inside a rice cooker or a smart TV. At the end of the showcase, their teacher declares that combining ideas from every term of the year -- not just remembering them one at a time -- is the true mark of everything Year 1 Computing set out to teach.",
