        passageEn:
            "For today's challenge, Nay Chi's robot starts at the classroom door and needs to reach her desk in the back corner. She thinks carefully and writes down each step in order.\n\n\"Forward three steps, turn right, forward two steps,\" she writes, testing it out loud with Moe Moe and Htet Htet listening. The robot rolls forward three times, turns to face a new direction, then rolls forward two more times, arriving exactly at her desk.\n\nHtet Htet tries his own set of directions for a different robot to reach the window, but he accidentally writes \"forward two steps, right\" -- forgetting the final \"forward one step\" needed to actually reach the window after turning. His robot turns at the right spot but stops one step short.\n\nThe teacher reminds the class that step-by-step directions must include every step, in the exact order needed, or the robot will not reach its destination -- practicing this with a toy robot is exactly like writing a computer algorithm.",
