        passageEn:
            "For the term's final project, Moe Moe, Nay Chi, and Htet Htet must guide a toy robot through a maze from the classroom door to the reading corner, using only forward, backward, left, and right commands.\n\nThey plan their sequence carefully, step by step: forward two steps, turn right to go around the bookshelf, forward three steps, turn left to face the reading corner, then forward one more step to arrive.\n\nWhen they test it, the robot stops one step short of the reading corner. \"There's a bug,\" says Htet Htet. They check each step and realize they wrote \"forward\" instead of \"forward two\" for the last step -- the robot needed two more steps, not one.\n\nThey debug their directions by fixing the last step to \"forward two,\" and this time the robot rolls perfectly into the reading corner. Their teacher congratulates them on combining three whole terms' worth of skills: giving directional commands, writing a correct step-by-step sequence, and debugging a mistake to fix it.",
