        titleEn: "Zaw Zaw's Backwards Program",
        titleMy: "ဇော်ဇော်၏ ပြောင်းပြန် Program",
        passageEn:
            "The next week, the teacher gave the class a new challenge: guide the character to a flag that sat two steps to the right and one step down from where it started. Zaw Zaw quickly snapped together a Move Down block, a Move Right block, and a Move Right block, in that exact order, and pressed play.\n\nBut something went wrong. His character moved down one step first, then right, then right again -- and it landed just short of the flag, on the wrong square. \"That's strange,\" said Zaw Zaw, looking closely at his screen. \"I used the right blocks, but the flag isn't where my character ended up.\"\n\nMoe Moe leaned over and looked at his stack of blocks. \"Your blocks are correct,\" she said, \"but look at the order. You moved down first, so your Right blocks moved you across a lower row than the flag is on.\" Zaw Zaw compared his stack with the picture of the flag's exact position and realised Moe Moe was right -- the flag needed him to move right twice first, and only then move down.\n\nZaw Zaw unsnapped his blocks and put them back together in the new order: Move Right, Move Right, then Move Down. This time, when he pressed play, his character slid across and landed perfectly on the flag. \"Same three blocks,\" he said, grinning, \"just a different order -- and that changed everything.\"",
