      readingPassage: ReadingPassageModel(
        titleEn: "Nay Chi's Tired Fingers",
        titleMy: "နေချည်၏ ပင်ပန်းသော လက်ချောင်းများ",
        passageEn:
            "The teacher's new challenge was to move the character five steps to the right, all the way across the grid. Nay Chi got to work, clicking the Move Right block from the toolbox and dragging it into her program. Then she clicked it again. And again. And again. And again.\n\n\"My fingers are getting tired,\" Nay Chi said, after dragging the fifth Move Right block into place. \"There must be an easier way than placing the same block five separate times.\" Moe Moe, sitting next to her, smiled and pointed at a new block in the toolbox shaped like an open loop. \"That's the repeat block,\" she said. \"You put a number in it, and it runs whatever is inside it that many times.\"\n\nNay Chi deleted her five separate Move Right blocks and dragged out a single repeat block instead. She typed the number 5 into it, then dragged just one Move Right block inside the loop. \"So instead of five blocks, I only need two: the repeat block and one Move Right block inside it?\" she asked. \"Exactly,\" said Moe Moe. \"The loop does the repeating for you.\"\n\nNay Chi pressed play, and her character slid smoothly across all five steps, landing exactly where the five separate blocks would have taken it -- but this time, her program looked much shorter and neater. \"A loop block saves so much time,\" she said, \"and my fingers thank you, Moe Moe!\"",
